	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Report Dropbox spam / fraud / phishing links without logging in.

Setup
  Open the workflow's Configuration and set "Your email" (required) and,
  optionally, "Your name". These are sent as the reporter details on the
  Dropbox abuse form.

Usage
  1. Trigger Alfred and type:  report-abuse &lt;dropbox-link&gt;
  2. Choose a category: phishing, fraud, or abuse.
  3. Press Enter. A notification confirms whether Dropbox accepted the report.

How it works
  Dropbox's public report form (dropbox.com/report_abuse/submit) uses a
  double-submit-cookie CSRF check. The workflow first GETs a Dropbox page to
  obtain the __Host-js_csrf cookie, then POSTs the report echoing that value
  back in the `t` field. No login or API key is required.</string>
